{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1119151-project-wtchr-lost-boys-minor-template-hack","id":1119151,"title":"PROJECT: WTCHR (Lost Boys Minor Template hack)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-21T20:02:37-07:00","id":1119151,"title":"PROJECT: WTCHR (Lost Boys Minor Template hack)","content":"PROJECT: WTCHR<br /> <br /> I'm a fan of super-soldier concepts, from the heroic (Captain America &lt;3) to the less so (Deathstroke <i>et al</i>.) <i>Hurt Locker</i>'s Lost Boys adapted the idea to the Chronicles of Darkness. In the process, it made a very specific choice to center the concept around themes of addiction, dependency, and mystery (just what <i>is </i>Delta Protocol, and how far will you go to secure your next shipment of Serum?)<br /> <br /> I'm not posting this to knock that choice; it makes for good drama. But addiction isn't the only dramatically-compelling driver for these characters, and it may not be one every table wants to explore. Consider the <i>Witcher </i>franchise: in broad strokes, it's the story of monster-hunters who, despite their superhuman abilities, are often outmatched by their chosen &quot;prey.&quot; They're too few and far between, in part because the process that makes them is often fatal, and they're confronted with elder evils they don't fully comprehend... but they keep going anyway. Sometimes because they get paid; sometimes because those elder evils threaten people they love; sometimes simply because there is no one else, and they'd rather risk their own lives than stand by and watch human beings disappear down some monster's jaws.<br /> <br /> Put that way, it sounds not unlike a third-tier game of <i>Hunter: The Vigil</i>, complete with ethical dilemmas about how to treat more the humane monsters that just want to be left alone, lingering doubts about how &quot;human&quot; you still are when you can live a hundred years and see in the dark, and razor-edged temptations to push your enhancements past the point of wisdom. So I wanted to offer a quick minor-template hack for the Lost Boys, changing their thematic focus while leaving the superhuman mechanics largely in place.<br /> <br /> Finally: I'm eagerly awaiting <i>HtV 2nd Ed.</i> and <i>Deviant: The Renegades</i>. It's my hope that either or both of those books will create official rules to more fully express this concept in play. Until then, however, homebrewed adaptations will have to suffice. Feedback is welcome.<br /> <br /> Minor Template: WTCHR (\u25cf - \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)<br /> <br /> You survived PROJECT: WTCHR (Weaponized Transhuman Combat Heuristic Redesign). You're still <i>you</i>, more or less, but a core-to-sheath combination of bionics, cybernetic implants, and even (it's rumored) transplanted bits and pieces of monsters have made you stronger, faster, and more enduring. It's <i>almost</i> enough to let you keep up with the things that go bump in the night.<br /> <br /> You gain the Supernatural Resistance, Augmented Resilience, Augmented Speed, Strength Augmentation, and Uncanny Perception Merits at one dot each. If you increase your dots in WTCHR (cost: 5 XP/dot), these Merits also increase, up to their individual maximums. You may buy the other Augmentation Merits (<i>Hurt Locker</i>, pgs. 97-100) at their usual cost. You are immune to Lunacy, Quiescence, and similar effects. You do not need the Serum and do not experience the Deprived Condition.<br /> <br /> You can activate the &quot;Deprived&quot; effect of any Augmentation - &quot;overclocking&quot; - by spending 1 Willpower. At the end of any scene in which you do so, roll Resolve + WTCHR - the number of Augmentations you &quot;overclocked.&quot; On an exceptional success, you take no damage; ordinary success triggers 1 Bashing per overclock; on failure, 1 Lethal/overclock; on <i>dramatic </i>failure, 1 Aggravated/overclock. (Push your augmentations too far past their limits, and the crash might kill you even if the gremlins don't.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13570-amusedbyirony","name":"AmusedByIrony","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T20:12:55-07:00","id":1119152,"title":"","content":"Addendum, because it's not a proper <i>Witcher </i>story until you can bring a sword to a gunfight: <br /> <br /> Augmentation Merit: Bullet Time (\u25cf\u25cf)<br /> <br /> Prerequisites: Augmented Speed 1, Uncanny Perception 1<br /> Effect: Use the higher of your Wits &amp; Dexterity to calculate Defense.<br /> Deprived: Apply Defense against Firearms attacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13570-amusedbyirony","name":"AmusedByIrony","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T02:52:29-07:00","id":1119813,"title":"","content":"This is great. Maybe you could add something about how the physically look different or maybe an aura of weirdness as disadvantages something like each augmentation they have cause something about them to seem off making social roles harder and intimation easier. In the games Geralt was always being spotted because of his eyes maybe they all have to wear sunglasses so they don.t freak people out hence the men in black uniform. Good ideal though I didnt really like the drug part but couldnt think of a good way of keeping the overclock mechanic with out it so thanks! Though depending on how much you want to keep the Witcher theme you could have it where the overclock is caused by drinking a pre prepared potion with or without willpower with a toxicity role based on the merit dots of the merit your overcloking. So you would have to think ahead instead of just reacting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11277,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11277-hyperspacewizard","user":"hyperspacewizard","date":". 07-24-2017, 05:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11277-hyperspacewizard","name":"hyperspacewizard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11277_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T03:42:59-07:00","id":1119826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hyperspacewizard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1119151-project-wtchr-lost-boys-minor-template-hack?p=1119813#post1119813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is great. Maybe you could add something about how the physically look different or maybe an aura of weirdness as disadvantages something like each augmentation they have cause something about them to seem off making social roles harder and intimation easier. In the games Geralt was always being spotted because of his eyes maybe they all have to wear sunglasses so they don.t freak people out hence the men in black uniform. Good ideal though I didnt really like the drug part but couldnt think of a good way of keeping the overclock mechanic with out it so thanks! Though depending on how much you want to keep the Witcher theme you could have it where the overclock is caused by drinking a pre prepared potion with or without willpower with a toxicity role based on the merit dots of the merit your overcloking. So you would have to think ahead instead of just reacting.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you wanted to do it similarly, you could even drop the potion an refluff it as &quot;pushing your cybernetics leads to toxic byproducts&quot;. The inbuilt systems can handle the typical operation, but over-clocking strains your biology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}